/// The project's CI on GitHub Actions, for any kind of app: go vet, the tests
/// (the runner has Docker, for testcontainers), the build, and a check that
/// the generated code is what the model generates (esquadro gen -check, with
/// the esquadro version of the lockfile). With docker, on tags v*, it builds
/// the image and publishes it to GitHub's container registry
/// (ghcr.io/<owner>/<repo>). It runs as little as it can, to save Actions
/// minutes: pushes to the long-lived branches only (pull requests cover the
/// others), no runs for draft pull requests, older runs cancelled.
blueprint github_actions {
  version "0.1.0"
  requires app
  optional docker

  /// Branches whose pushes run the CI, as items of a YAML list, e.g.
  /// main, develop, "release/**"; main when nobody contributes.
  slot "github_actions.branches"
  /// Steps run first in the test job, as YAML indented by six spaces, e.g.
  /// a check of the pull request's branch name.
  slot "github_actions.test.steps"
  /// Jobs of the CI workflow, as YAML indented by two spaces. Each job is
  /// billed by the minute, rounded up: prefer a step of the test job.
  slot "github_actions.jobs"
}
